From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Arun Iyengar <aiyengar1990@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 11:10:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/4] drm/bridge: dw-hdmi: Attach the color format property

When a bridge in front of dw-hdmi takes part in the bus format
selection, dw-hdmi offers RGB, YUV 4:4:4, YUV 4:2:2 and YUV 4:2:0 output
formats, but the connector it creates has no way for userspace to pick
one: the first entry that the chain accepts is always used. The DRM
core has a "color format" connector property for that, and the bridge
chain already skips bus formats that do not match the requested one.

Attach it, with YUV 4:2:0 only where the connector allows it, when
the output format is negotiated. When dw-hdmi is the first or only
bridge its output is fixed, so the property is not attached there.

Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Arun Iyengar <aiyengar1990@gmail.com>
---
diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/bridge/synopsys/dw-hdmi.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/bridge/synopsys/dw-hdmi.c
index 5f26c81..d3a9ddc 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/bridge/synopsys/dw-hdmi.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/bridge/synopsys/dw-hdmi.c
@@ -2748,6 +2748,24 @@ static int dw_hdmi_connector_create(struct dw_hdmi *hdmi)
 
 	drm_connector_attach_max_bpc_property(connector, 8, 16);
 
+	/*
+	 * The output format is only negotiated when a bridge in front of
+	 * this one takes part in the bus format selection; otherwise the
+	 * output is fixed to RGB and a color format request has no effect.
+	 */
+	if (!list_is_singular(&hdmi->bridge.encoder->bridge_chain) &&
+	    !list_is_first(&hdmi->bridge.chain_node,
+			   &hdmi->bridge.encoder->bridge_chain)) {
+		unsigned long formats = BIT(DRM_OUTPUT_COLOR_FORMAT_RGB444) |
+					BIT(DRM_OUTPUT_COLOR_FORMAT_YCBCR444) |
+					BIT(DRM_OUTPUT_COLOR_FORMAT_YCBCR422);
+
+		if (connector->ycbcr_420_allowed)
+			formats |= BIT(DRM_OUTPUT_COLOR_FORMAT_YCBCR420);
+
+		drm_connector_attach_color_format_property(connector, formats);
+	}
+
 	if (hdmi->version >= 0x200a && hdmi->plat_data->use_drm_infoframe) {
 		drm_connector_attach_hdr_output_metadata_property(connector);
 
